ECOMM APP - AMAZING ANIMAL PAINTING:
- ng g module product
- ng g service product/product (product service connected to product module)
- ng g component product/product-list

Class:
- "ng g class models/product"
creates product class under models folder

-> redirect home to products
const routes: Routes = [
  {path:'', redirectTo:'/products',pathMatch:'full'},
  {path:'products',component:ProductListComponent}
];

ENVIRONMENTS:
- since ang v15 , they are not getting created automatically
- "ng g environments"
- environments/environment.development.ts:
    export const environment = {
        apiUrl: 'http://localhost:3000'
    };
in angular.json:
    - we can see in development env replaces .ts with development.ts
            "development": {
                {
                  "replace": "src/environments/environment.ts",
                  "with": "src/environments/environment.development.ts"
                }
            }

to start env in diff configurations:
- "ng serve --configuration=development"

Angular Materials and exporting Cards:
(angular.material.dev)
    - angular material imporves styling and user exp.
    "ng add @angular/material"

    - when we want to use any angular material component, we have to pick the module where we want to import it
    (check api for that component , can copy paste the import from website directly)
        import {MatCardModule} from '@angular/material/card';
    
    -in html:
        <mat-card class="product-card">....

Images:
assets/images

To use angular material theme:
    - check angular.json for styles:
        "styles": [
              "@angular/material/prebuilt-themes/indigo-pink.css",
              "src/styles.css"
            ],
    - import it to styles.css (global) 
        @import "@angular/material/prebuilt-themes/indigo-pink.css";

Responsive Grids:
- angular meterial grids doesnt have responsiveness
- we can use flexLayout https://github.com/angular/flex-layout 
